.TH ASIKA 1 "2026-05-09" "Asika" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asika \- Asika PR Manager CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asika
[OPTIONS] COMMAND [SUBCOMMAND] [ARGUMENTS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Asika is a multi-platform pull request management tool. The CLI interacts with the asikad daemon to manage PRs across GitHub, GitLab, Gitea, Forgejo, Codeberg, and Bitbucket from a single interface.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " token"
.BI \-\-token " token"
JWT token or API key for authentication.
Can also be set via
.B ASIKA_TOKEN
environment variable.
.TP
.BI \-s " url"
.BI \-\-server " url"
asikad server address (default: http://localhost:8080).
Can also be set via
.B ASIKA_SERVER
environment variable.
.TP
.BI \-o " format"
.BI \-\-output " format"
Output format: table, json, yaml (default: table).
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.TP
.B asika login [-\-username <user>] [-\-password <pass>] [-\-save]
Login with username/password to obtain JWT token. Use
.B \-\-save
to persist credentials to ~/.config/asika/config.json.
.TP
.B asika login \-\-api-key <key> [-\-save]
Save an API key directly (e.g. from WebUI). No username/password needed.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS asika completion
Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell.
.TP
Usage:
.B asika completion
[bash|zsh|fish|powershell]
.SS asika config
Manage asikad configuration.
.TP
.B asika config show
Show current config (secrets masked).
.TP
.B asika config set
[\-\-file " path"]
Set config from file or stdin (TOML format).
.TP
.B asika config reload
Trigger hot reload of config.
.SS asika init
Run configuration wizard (sends setup to server).
.SS asika login
Login to asikad and save token for future requests.
See AUTHENTICATION above.
.SS asika pr
Manage pull requests.
.TP
.B asika pr list
[group] [\-\-state open|closed|merged] [\-\-platform github|gitlab|gitea]
[\-\-is_draft true|false] [\-\-author " name"]
[\-\-label " label"] [\-\-created_after " time"]
[\-\-updated_after " time"] [\-\-page " n"] [\-\-per_page " n"]
List PRs with filters.
.TP
.B asika pr show
[group] [id]
Show PR details.
.TP
.B asika pr approve
[group] [id]
Approve PR.
.TP
.B asika pr close
[group] [id]
Close PR.
.TP
.B asika pr reopen
[group] [id]
Reopen PR.
.TP
.B asika pr spam
[group] [id] [\-\-undo]
Mark/unmark as spam.
.TP
.B asika pr comment
[group] [id] [body]
Comment on PR.
.TP
.B asika pr rebase
[group] [id]
Rebase PR onto base branch.
.TP
.B asika pr cherry-pick
[group] [id] <target-branch>
Cherry-pick merged PR.
.TP
.B asika pr batch\-approve
[group] [id1,id2,...]
Batch approve PRs.
.TP
.B asika pr batch\-close
[group] [id1,id2,...]
Batch close PRs.
.TP
.B asika pr batch\-label
[group] [id1,id2,...] \-\-label " name" [\-\-color " hex"]
Batch add label to PRs.
.SS asika queue
Manage merge queue.
.TP
.B asika queue list
[group]
Show merge queue.
.TP
.B asika queue recheck
[group]
Trigger queue recheck.
.TP
.B asika queue clear
[group]
Clear all queue items.
.TP
.B asika queue remove
<group> <id>
Remove specific PR from queue.
.SS asika apikey
Manage API keys (admin only).
.TP
.B asika apikey create <name> <role>
Create a new API key. Role: admin, operator, viewer.
Returns the raw key (shown once).
.TP
.B asika apikey list
List all API keys (raw secrets not shown).
.TP
.B asika apikey revoke <key_id>
Revoke an API key.
.SS asika user
Manage users (admin only).
.TP
.B asika user list
List all users.
.TP
.B asika user add <username> \-\-password <pwd> \-\-role <role> [\-\-groups <g1,g2>] [\-\-permissions <p1,p2>]
Create a new user.
Roles: admin, operator, viewer.
Permissions: approve, merge, close, reopen, spam, queue.
.TP
.B asika user update <username> [\-\-password <pwd>] [\-\-role <role>] [\-\-groups <g1,g2>] [\-\-permissions <p1,p2>] [\-\-no\-perms <p1,p2>]
Update an existing user.
.TP
.B asika user delete <username>
Delete a user.
.SS asika rules
Manage label rules (auto-labeling by file patterns).
.TP
.B asika rules list
List label rules.
.TP
.B asika rules add <pattern> <label>
Add label rule.
.TP
.B asika rules remove <pattern>
Remove label rule.
.SS asika self\-update
Update asika/asikad to the latest version.
.TP
Options:
[\-\-version " tag"] [\-\-check] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-yes] [\-\-rollback] [\-\-restart]
.TP
Examples:
.B asika self\-update \-\-check
.br
.B asika self\-update
.br
.B asika self\-update \-\-rollback
.SS asika stale
Manage stale PRs.
.TP
.B asika stale check
[group] [\-\-dry\-run]
Check for stale PRs.
.TP
.B asika stale unmark
[group] [id]
Remove stale label.
.SS asika sync
Manage sync history (multi mode).
.TP
.B asika sync history
Show sync history.
.TP
.B asika sync retry
[sync_id]
Retry failed sync.
.SS asika stats
Show DORA metrics and overview statistics.
.SS asika usage
Show real-time CPU and memory usage.
.SS asika version
Print version information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ASIKA_TOKEN
JWT token or API key for authentication.
.TP
.B ASIKA_SERVER
asikad server address.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/asika/config.json
CLI configuration file storing token and server settings.
.I /etc/asika_config.toml
Server configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asikad (1)
\- Asika daemon documentation.
.SH AUTHORS
Asika Project.
